[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-107937"] :question/problem "The second-order differential equation ${y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}+y=0$\ncan be expressed as the matrix equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where \n\n$$\nx(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}],\\,y(t)={x}_{1}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)={x}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\nFind the matrix $A.$" :question/worked-solution "We first need to express the given differential equation as a system of first-order differential equations. Then, we write the system as a matrix equation.\n\nWe start by making the following change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =y \\\\ {x}_{2} & ={y}^{′}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equations with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′} & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′} & ={y}^{″}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={y}^{″}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now write the right-hand side of the last equation in terms of ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}.$\n\nSolving our original differential equation for the highest-order derivative $({y}^{″}),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=2{y}^{′}-y.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute our new variables into the right-hand side of the above equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=2{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}.\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not include any derivative terms on the right-hand side. \n\nTherefore, our complete system of equations is as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}=-{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can represent this system as the matrix differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence, $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-109635/selection/b35d01a3dfe1edd8104f9b5d6dc35739c0c87d15a49dbd72501dfa8b007e2719" :answer/id #uuid "6b4c0797-21eb-5f1e-9ea3-8f99dee48abb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16({x}_{1}+4{x}_{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109635/selection/09f588b1d3568a65cf3079d49ef6cec24801ee92c5d45ffccacdad2a7c4a0a61" :answer/id #uuid "dd0d3599-6297-59ce-8a64-c99e931a4330" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8(2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109635/selection/749981ac18a11da59ed54013056eb926ad552c50b2aa8a3286b801987f5427eb" :answer/id #uuid "c1ad7f3e-4506-5467-b6a0-c04078ff1bab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16(2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109635/selection/45cb4b44744dcda154f31f9a768aa887a86ebb99aeefaf3d65bda3cf09ffe8a7" :answer/id #uuid "5fee1643-0534-59f5-a028-0f614a9bbcda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6({x}_{1}-2{x}_{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109635/selection/11eedc2e11ac63a60e9a26ffc7ec4e3defba49b5b3dd4d8cda69c1c574927596" :answer/id #uuid "adc5b24c-fc24-5d47-b284-477597052b8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4(2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109635/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "725311ef-1f3d-5db4-adca-0f73a6abd290" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109635/selection/749981ac18a11da59ed54013056eb926ad552c50b2aa8a3286b801987f5427eb" :answer-field/choices ["q-109635/selection/b35d01a3dfe1edd8104f9b5d6dc35739c0c87d15a49dbd72501dfa8b007e2719" "q-109635/selection/09f588b1d3568a65cf3079d49ef6cec24801ee92c5d45ffccacdad2a7c4a0a61" "q-109635/selection/749981ac18a11da59ed54013056eb926ad552c50b2aa8a3286b801987f5427eb" "q-109635/selection/45cb4b44744dcda154f31f9a768aa887a86ebb99aeefaf3d65bda3cf09ffe8a7" "q-109635/selection/11eedc2e11ac63a60e9a26ffc7ec4e3defba49b5b3dd4d8cda69c1c574927596"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109635" :question/id #uuid "b332ac9d-e1aa-5efa-b417-32a7d962209b" :question/math-academy-id "q-109635" :question/problem "The second-order initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-8{y}^{′}-16y=0,\\,y(1)=3,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=1\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2},\\, & {x}_{1}(1)=p \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}=f(t),\\, & {x}_{2}(1)=q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}(t)=y(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t)={y}^{′}(t),$ and $p$ and $q$ are constants. Calculate  $(p-q)\\cdot f(t).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the following change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =y \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={y}^{′}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also convert the initial conditions, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & ={x}_{1}(1)=3 \\\\ {y}^{′}(1) & ={x}_{2}(1)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equations with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{″}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={y}^{″}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt this point, we're almost done. We just need to write the right-hand side of the last equation in terms of ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}.$\n\nSolving our original differential equation for the highest-order derivative $({y}^{″}),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=8{y}^{′}+16y.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute our new variables into the right-hand side of the above equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=8{x}_{2}+16{x}_{1}.\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not include any derivative terms on the right-hand side. \n\nTherefore, our complete system of equations is as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2},\\, & {x}_{1}(1)=3 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}=16{x}_{1}+8{x}_{2},\\, & {x}_{2}(1)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $p=3,q=1,f(t)=16{x}_{1}+8{x}_{2},$ and \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(p+q)\\cdot f(t) & =(3-1)(16{x}_{1}+8{x}_{2}) \\\\  & =2(8)(2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}) \\\\  & =16(2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-109635/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c19ef7ec-19a3-533a-bcd9-1b775f301801"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109635"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109636/selection/c9ee11d0dafc0f795a2105874ffd6e1df8258b75f71216d34105c1f4800380c1" :answer/id #uuid "839f1a25-3851-5a20-af1e-3a5c6d4af041" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109636/selection/355fa0ac0120b8df902f94e48512bf36f1d6fed3405ce96493af65a92cd3e5f0" :answer/id #uuid "771c8137-7dd9-5758-bb0a-ffc6dc52d469" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12(3{x}_{1}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{x}_{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109636/selection/c87733e331741824a6c396dcc99e0dfadbcab63c321fde5c825b5529910048ad" :answer/id #uuid "bf6d2c00-369a-5efc-b831-acbe6746bb70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12(3{x}_{1}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{x}_{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109636/selection/d41c5698eae24fe13953fe77b922915ddad5d1fa08b7f2dc9d125948dc030ac1" :answer/id #uuid "a35bcfa7-f0d1-5df7-a71d-27c1b0711d93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109636/selection/a863074647ef97e9f0c55f0614bb539e712514be91c3f95c16af0793e093b463" :answer/id #uuid "82b63a8a-38e3-5ba5-bd8a-89d58d436f7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-15(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109636/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9497cbb4-0690-57c4-8ade-12f260987f50" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109636/selection/d41c5698eae24fe13953fe77b922915ddad5d1fa08b7f2dc9d125948dc030ac1" :answer-field/choices ["q-109636/selection/c9ee11d0dafc0f795a2105874ffd6e1df8258b75f71216d34105c1f4800380c1" "q-109636/selection/355fa0ac0120b8df902f94e48512bf36f1d6fed3405ce96493af65a92cd3e5f0" "q-109636/selection/c87733e331741824a6c396dcc99e0dfadbcab63c321fde5c825b5529910048ad" "q-109636/selection/d41c5698eae24fe13953fe77b922915ddad5d1fa08b7f2dc9d125948dc030ac1" "q-109636/selection/a863074647ef97e9f0c55f0614bb539e712514be91c3f95c16af0793e093b463"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109636" :question/id #uuid "14da67e4-ca85-5189-99d0-c71c3051d763" :question/math-academy-id "q-109636" :question/problem "The second-order initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-10{y}^{′}+25\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,y=0,\\,y(0)=-1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=2\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2},\\, & {x}_{1}(0)=p \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}=f(t),\\, & {x}_{2}(0)=q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}(t)=y(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t)={y}^{′}(t),$ and $p$ and $q$ are constants. Calculate  $(p-q)\\cdot f(t).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the following change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =y \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={y}^{′}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also convert the initial conditions, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & ={x}_{1}(0)=-1 \\\\ {y}^{′}(0) & ={x}_{2}(0)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equations with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{″}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={y}^{″}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt this point, we're almost done. We just need to write the right-hand side of the last equation in terms of ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}.$\n\nSolving our original differential equation for the highest-order derivative $({y}^{″}),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=10{y}^{′}-25\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,y.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute our new variables into the right-hand side of the above equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=10{x}_{2}-25\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{x}_{1}.\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not include any derivative terms on the right-hand side. \n\nTherefore, our complete system of equations is as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2},\\, & {x}_{1}(0)=-1 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}=-25\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{x}_{1}+10{x}_{2},\\, & {x}_{2}(0)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $p=-1,q=2,f(t)=-25\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{x}_{1}+10{x}_{2},$ and \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(p-q)\\cdot f(t) & =(-1-2)(-25\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{x}_{1}+10{x}_{2}) \\\\  & =-3(-5)(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}) \\\\  & =15(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-109636/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c19ef7ec-19a3-533a-bcd9-1b775f301801"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109636"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109644/selection/23c415882de7cf10b3f45062a050619054c0d7b8bece9a7d227f38663bf8a26e" :answer/id #uuid "2d46168f-7a0f-5a78-a880-016a6fa26e4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{x}_{1}+2{x}_{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109644/selection/2fd1bc142a4f55900ebbcd3442070f28bb3bf7fc07eaa0a662d6f6a960907381" :answer/id #uuid "92641ae3-ff7f-5ada-b77c-5049af5554ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109644/selection/034b5ea602cdc0e99077abf0714683caf3f2c588dece633a61e99608804648d0" :answer/id #uuid "053bf2a5-aa50-57aa-85b2-20427a62051d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109644/selection/b503f4d767d80cb294c5d995761f16e5a15ff968f0c6b86651cda7855dcd7842" :answer/id #uuid "2c4714dc-008f-5ac2-a284-b33923b09bbe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109644/selection/fef4bc54d85651c32b7ce8cee03206c9de3e994b9fa02c6e29474bbbcfcdedc0" :answer/id #uuid "a920502b-11cb-572d-9404-2a028ce878c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109644/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9479ba64-af75-5aa3-8f16-b5502d6effe6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109644/selection/b503f4d767d80cb294c5d995761f16e5a15ff968f0c6b86651cda7855dcd7842" :answer-field/choices ["q-109644/selection/23c415882de7cf10b3f45062a050619054c0d7b8bece9a7d227f38663bf8a26e" "q-109644/selection/2fd1bc142a4f55900ebbcd3442070f28bb3bf7fc07eaa0a662d6f6a960907381" "q-109644/selection/034b5ea602cdc0e99077abf0714683caf3f2c588dece633a61e99608804648d0" "q-109644/selection/b503f4d767d80cb294c5d995761f16e5a15ff968f0c6b86651cda7855dcd7842" "q-109644/selection/fef4bc54d85651c32b7ce8cee03206c9de3e994b9fa02c6e29474bbbcfcdedc0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109644" :question/id #uuid "4d721395-7f60-58c6-8c94-e984d75af312" :question/math-academy-id "q-109644" :question/problem "The third-order initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}+{y}^{″}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,y=0,\\,y(0)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-1,\\,{y}^{″}(0)=4\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2},\\, & {x}_{1}(0)=p \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3},\\, & {x}_{2}(0)=q \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}=f(t),\\, & {x}_{3}(0)=r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}(t)=y(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t)={y}^{′}(t),$ ${x}_{3}(t)={y}^{″}(t),$ and $p,$ $q$ and $r$ are constants. Calculate  $(p-q-r)\\cdot f(t).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the following change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =y \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{3}(t) & ={y}^{″}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also convert the initial conditions, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & ={x}_{1}(0)=2 \\\\ {y}^{′}(0) & ={x}_{2}(0)=-1 \\\\ {y}^{″}(0) & ={x}_{3}(0)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equations with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{″} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{‴}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3}, \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}={y}^{‴}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt this point, we're almost done. We just need to write the right-hand side of the last equation in terms of ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}.$\n\nSolving our original differential equation for the highest-order derivative $({y}^{‴}),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}=-{y}^{″}+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,y.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute our new variables into the right-hand side of the above equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}=-{x}_{3}+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{x}_{1}.\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not include any derivative terms on the right-hand side. \n\nTherefore, our complete system of equations is as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2},\\, & {x}_{1}(0)=2 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3},\\, & {x}_{2}(0)=-1 \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{x}_{1}-{x}_{3},\\, & {x}_{3}(0)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $p=2,q=-1,r=4,f(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{x}_{1}-{x}_{3},$ and \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(p-q-r)\\cdot f(t) & =(2-(-1)-4)(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{x}_{1}-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =(2+1-4)(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{x}_{1}-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =(-1)(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{x}_{1}-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109644/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c19ef7ec-19a3-533a-bcd9-1b775f301801"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109644"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109691/selection/48d1910f76a89212dd53357be70d7553c02f0bcae2eeaceb55a7991e8db40ecf" :answer/id #uuid "a6d18008-e207-53a1-ba40-56d636e8c410" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4{t}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 5t\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109691/selection/ed2889034e228b6cb0beabb2e28b3ee69ce5c1e9c7ef9ad493916f4f3385f4f1" :answer/id #uuid "35e54c5c-1bd8-5865-98fa-50638187c3bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & t \\\\ 4{t}^{3} & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109691/selection/e46eb02f5629d55d1be3bf714a93bbf647d8367f98b66e905c7d22b00abf8c90" :answer/id #uuid "f5eb5139-cba2-5ac2-a1e8-d7c9a5e36ac7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 5t & 4{t}^{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109691/selection/d766323db6d1ee5bb74330150fa043c2cc8cfa348a57dc72ba16718fcba1d677" :answer/id #uuid "d1cc7177-6b1e-5e45-84e6-95d9a0050f3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4{t}^{3} & 5t\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109691/selection/6efa38bc808215347d4890900cf55301e290976f78af272c0cd05e177d3ade32" :answer/id #uuid "1acd58de-5aa6-51de-a3c9-9bb6e738a243" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -5t & 4{t}^{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109691/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fa4c4df5-9c6d-5917-9761-8b56610953b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109691/selection/e46eb02f5629d55d1be3bf714a93bbf647d8367f98b66e905c7d22b00abf8c90" :answer-field/choices ["q-109691/selection/48d1910f76a89212dd53357be70d7553c02f0bcae2eeaceb55a7991e8db40ecf" "q-109691/selection/ed2889034e228b6cb0beabb2e28b3ee69ce5c1e9c7ef9ad493916f4f3385f4f1" "q-109691/selection/e46eb02f5629d55d1be3bf714a93bbf647d8367f98b66e905c7d22b00abf8c90" "q-109691/selection/d766323db6d1ee5bb74330150fa043c2cc8cfa348a57dc72ba16718fcba1d677" "q-109691/selection/6efa38bc808215347d4890900cf55301e290976f78af272c0cd05e177d3ade32"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109691" :question/id #uuid "9a927c15-49d0-5bb3-a29e-68798842c0ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-109691" :question/problem "The second-order differential equation ${y}^{″}-4{t}^{3}{y}^{′}-5ty=0$\ncan be expressed as the matrix equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where \n\n$$\nx(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}],\\,y(t)={x}_{1}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)={x}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\nFind the matrix $A.$" :question/worked-solution "We first need to express the given differential equation as a system of first-order differential equations. Then, we write the system as a matrix equation.\n\nWe start by making the following change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =y \\\\ {x}_{2} & ={y}^{′}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equations with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′} & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′} & ={y}^{″}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={y}^{″}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now write the right-hand side of the last equation in terms of ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}.$\n\nSolving our original differential equation for the highest-order derivative $({y}^{″}),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=4{t}^{3}{y}^{′}+5ty.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute our new variables into the right-hand side of the above equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=4{t}^{3}{x}_{2}+5t{x}_{1}.\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not include any derivative terms on the right-hand side. \n\nTherefore, our complete system of equations is as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}=5t{x}_{1}+4{t}^{3}{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can represent this system as the matrix differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 5t & 4{t}^{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence, $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 5t & 4{t}^{3}\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-109691/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7657ff9-3918-5080-b9a2-8f6a6d8b4fd9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109691"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
